   929	The presheaf \(\Pic^\sharp_{C/k}\) is not \emph{a priori} a sheaf (Kleiman
   930	\S 2, L1330), and over a general field it is not representable: Kleiman states
   931	this outright at L5105--L5108 for the conic \(u^2+v^2+w^2=0\) in
   932	\(\I P^2_\bb R\) --- a smooth plane conic, hence smooth, proper and
   933	geometrically integral, over a field where it has no rational point ---
   934	because \(\Pic_{(X/\bb R)\et}\) is representable by \S 4 while the two
   935	functors differ (Exercise \texttt{ex:Pfs}).
